plaintext
* Transistors
M1 6 8 0 0 NMOS
M2 3 7 0 0 NMOS

* Current Source
IREF 2 6 DC

* Voltage Source
VDD 2 0 DC

* Node Mapping
* This section explains which nodes (1, 2, 3, etc.) are connected to which parts of the components.
* Node 0 is typically the ground in SPICE.

* Notes:
* - Node 2 is connected to VDD and the top of IREF.
* - Node 6 connects the bottom of IREF to the gate of M1.
* - Node 8 connects the drain of M1 to the gate of M2.
* - Node 3 is a common node connected to the source of M2, the drain of the NMOS in the top right.
* - Node 7 connects the gate of M2.
* - Node 5 is connected to the drain of the top right NMOS (indicated as B).

* NMOS Transistor:
* M<name> <drain> <gate> <source> <body> <model>